WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seemed like you focuse
your campaign

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.637 line:92%
on big structural changes.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, a disappointing end
to the campaign.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel, though,
optimistic about

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
how some of those messages
were received

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact that
the country does seem to b

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
moving to a more progressive
point of view,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
at least on some issues?
-Yeah, I do.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.026 size:88% position:44%
Yeah, I think that a lot
of what I talked about,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:29.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have now seen
in the middle of this crisis

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:30.930 size:78% position:39% line:92%
the importance of it.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, for example,
student-loan debt

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
is something that
is just crushing

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
hundreds of thousands
of young people

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just an enormous drag
on them.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:48.815
Social Security has not kept up.
Payments have not kept up.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.419
And we have not adjusted
the Social Security system

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
to ensure that it's gonna be
financially viable

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.724 line:92%
for long into the future.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:01.895
Those are two issues which i
talked about over and over

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:06.666
And in the middle of this
crisis, you really are reminded,

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.435 line:92%
students are supposed to b

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
making their
student-loan payments.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, finally,
we got into this bill

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have a six-month hiatus
on that.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
But think about it --
this is a time

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the federal governmen
could step in and say,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know what?
We can't keep dragging dow

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
both these young people
and our economy

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
by not having --
because they've got

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
these huge
student-loan debt burdens.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.994
So, it's something I want
to keep talking about.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.496 line:92%
Same thing on Social Security.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:40.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now is the time that we should
increase Social Security

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:45.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and disability payments
by $200 a month

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on into the future,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and restructure how
we pay for Social Security

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
so Social Security
is gonna last

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as we can see
into the future.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.351 size:78% position:39%
Those are the kind of
structural changes

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:02.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
that help support people
and help support our economy

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now that people
are under such pressure

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our economy
is under such pressure,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think a lot of folks
are giving ideas like that

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
a second look 'cause I think
they're really important.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.001 line:92%
It's a change we've got to make.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were a candidate
who was known for having plans

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
what seems like
a lifetime ago now

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.340 line:92%
but I believe was only January

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.843
You released a plan for how to
deal with infectious disease

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like coronavirus.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:28.014
Is this a plan you've considered
sending over to the White House?

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think
they would even look at it

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how was your plan differen
than the plan

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we've seen so far
out of D.C.?

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.959
-Well, you know, the main thin
about the plan is the timing

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:44.063
because when you're talkin
about a health crisis like this,

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.732 size:88% position:44% line:92%
like an economic crisis,

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
much more important
to get in front of it

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.370 line:92%
than chasing it from behind.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we had put in place
an effective plan

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:57.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
to deal with the coronavirus
back in January,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.778 line:92%
we would have saved lives.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we wouldn't put the stress
on our medical system

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're putting on it
right now

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.251 line:92%
and the stress on our economy.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:08.254
This is one of those thing
we should've made the mask

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the respirators and usin
all of the federal tools

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in January to get started
not chasing it.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.134
Here we are right at the end
of March, heading into April

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:24.237 size:88% position:44%
and still haven't done
much of what we need to.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:28.308
You know, for me, it's about -
it's what leadership is about.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:33.112
It's about seeing the kind
of threats to the country

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.249 size:78% position:39%
and seeing them early
and having a good,

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
thoughtful response to it,
having a plan for that.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's
what will guide this country

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.159 line:92%
and make this country safe

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.128 size:78% position:39%
and make this country
all that it can be.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being with us.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.933
We're gonna let you get back
to Bailey and your TV show

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all your other
important work.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
We hope to see you soon agai
back in the studio.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.105 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Really appreciate it.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Me too.
It's good to see you, too.

